  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "0.3.1 — CONFORMANCE FIX, upgrade recommended. Two deblocking bugs made the encoder's reconstruction diverge from a conformant decoder's: luma deblocking ignored the qP average across macroblock edges (ITU-T H.264 8.7.2.2), and inter boundary-strength derivation inverted the coefficient/motion-vector precedence (8.7.2.1). Both are masked at QP 23/28/33/34 — the values every prior decode-oracle test used — so they survived to release. Any stream at another QP drifts and compounds through the reference chain; constant-QP-31 output diverged ~8,000 pixels by frame 1 and ~23,000 by frame 5. AdaptiveQuantStrength and TargetBitsPerFrame are the most exposed, since both vary QP per macroblock. Verified byte-exact against ffmpeg and VideoToolbox. Bitstreams change only for the previously non-conformant configurations; constant-QP encodes at 23/28/33/34 are unaffected.",
